workedExamples.question_text:
A gardener recorded a seedling's height from week $2$ to week $7$. The scatterplot shows the observations and a line of best fit.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=1.5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{modelblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,xstep=6mm,ystep=7.5mm] (0,0) grid (10,35);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(10.5,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,36);
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.6);\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {5,10,15,20,25,30,35} {\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.15,\y);\path (0,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\foreach \p in {(2,9),(3,13),(4,14),(5,18),(6,20),(7,25)} {\fill[black] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\draw[modelblue,thick] (2,9)--(7,24);
\path (5,-6) node {Weeks since planting};
\path (-1.5,17.5) node[rotate=90] {Height (cm)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a. Use the line of best fit to predict the height at week $4$.

b. Use the line of best fit to predict when the height reaches $21$ cm.

c. Classify both predictions as interpolation or extrapolation.

