[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=1.5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{modelblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{guideorange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,xstep=6mm,ystep=7.5mm] (0,0) grid (10,30);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(10.5,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,31);
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.6);\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {5,10,15,20,25,30} {\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.15,\y);\path (0,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\foreach \p in {(3,12),(4,13),(5,17),(6,17),(7,21),(8,21)} {\fill[black] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\draw[modelblue,thick] (3,12)--(8,22);
\draw[modelblue,thick,dashed] (1,8)--(3,12);
\draw[modelblue,thick,dashed] (8,22)--(10,26);
\draw[guideorange,dashed,->] (1,0)--(1,8)--(0,8);
\draw[guideorange,dotted,->] (10,0)--(10,26)--(0,26);
\path (1,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$1$};
\path (0,8) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$8$};
\path (5,26) node[above,yshift=2mm] {26 cm};
\path (5,-6) node {Weeks since planting};
\path (-1.5,15) node[rotate=90] {Height (cm)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a. Extend the line backwards to week $1$: the predicted height is about $8$ cm. Extend it forwards to week $10$: the predicted height is about $26$ cm. Both are extrapolation because both weeks lie outside the recorded range of $3$ to $8$ weeks.

b. Week $5$ is generally more reliable. It is interpolation, supported by observations on both sides. Week $10$ assumes the growth trend continues beyond the observations.

c. Week $8.5$ is generally more reliable. Both predictions are extrapolation, but week $8.5$ is closer to the recorded range, so there is less opportunity for the growth trend to change.

